; fas9_cannoscale.scr - facit of 9.S (Codex 17, plan 9.17: the extents of the representation at the current annotation scale).
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_cannoscale.scr
; starts AutoCAD 2025's core on acad.dwt (a new empty drawing). Plain AutoCAD commands, no LISP (see fas9_example.scr).
;
; The drawing of fas9_contexts.scr as it is saved there (annotative TEXT, MTEXT, the dimensions, DIMJOGGED, DIMARC, LEADER, hatches and an
; annotative block's INSERT, each with the contexts 1:1 (the default), 1:2 and 1:5), then only the current annotation scale changes:
;   cannoscale            CANNOSCALE 1:1 (the default contexts: the entities' own fields)
;   cannoscale 1_2        CANNOSCALE HDXF_1_2, REGENALL: $EXTMIN/$EXTMAX of every object drawn by its 1:2 context
;   cannoscale 1_5        CANNOSCALE HDXF_1_5, REGENALL
; ANNOAUTOSCALE stays 0: no context is added (unlike fas9_contexts' autoscale, which also adds a 1:10 context to every object).
_.ANNOALLVISIBLE
1
_.ANNOAUTOSCALE
0
_.-SCALELISTEDIT
_Add
HDXF_1_2
1:2
_Exit
_.-SCALELISTEDIT
_Add
HDXF_1_5
1:5
_Exit
